//? Title: Transposed Convolution: Adjoint Geometry and Checkerboards
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Upsampling a feature map must place its coarse information on a finer grid. Transposed
convolution spreads filter-weighted contributions over that grid. We verify its adjoint
identity and show how overlap counts create checkerboards even on constant inputs.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/transposed_convolutions.cpp`.

> The method

For a fixed forward kernel, flatten convolution into y=Mx. Its input derivative is Mᵀg,
which defines transposed convolution. The filter layout is the original forward HWIO layout:
coarse channels equal its output channels. Specifying the fine output shape fixes stride and
padding ambiguity. The adjoint identity is

$$
\langle Mx,g\rangle=\langle x,M^Tg\rangle.
$$
\alttext(The forward output paired with an upstream tensor equals the input paired with the transposed-convolution output.)

An adjoint is not generally an inverse: downsampling loses information, and MᵀM is usually
not identity. At stride s, an all-one kernel of width k covers each interior phase either
floor(k/s) or ceil(k/s) times per axis. Counts are uniform when s divides k, but unequal learned
weights can still imbalance phases. Nearest-neighbour resize followed by ordinary convolution
preserves constants in the interior with a fixed filter. Edges must be analysed separately.
Each transposed operation has the same multiply-count order as the corresponding forward map.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/transposed_convolutions_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/transposed_convolutions_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/transposed_convolutions_concept.tikz > build/transposed_convolutions_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/transposed_convolutions_concept.svg build/transposed_convolutions_concept.dvi > build/transposed_convolutions_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
